.TH TUINK 1 "April 2026" "TUInk @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tuink \- terminal text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuink
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tuink
is a terminal text editor with syntax highlighting, search, multiple tabs,
and Git-aware gutter markers.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-mouse
Disable mouse tracking and mouse interactions.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-alt\-screen
Do not use the alternate screen buffer.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-color
Render without ANSI colors.
.TP
.BR \-\-theme= name
Select the UI palette: blue, cyan, or light.
.TP
.BR \-\-read
Start in reading mode with editing disabled.
.TP
.BR \-\-profile
Log render timings to standard error.
.TP
.BR \-\-profile\-file= path
Write render timings to a file and enable profiling.
.TP
.BR \-\-ui= tui
Select the terminal interface. The GUI target is not implemented.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tuink/tuink.properties
Per-user UI settings.
.SH AUTHORS
Dmitry Kosatchev.
